for the rights also required when using or rebuilding the combined app.

"Personal use" means use by an individual for their own activities.
"Internal use" means use within one organization (a single legal entity) by
its employees or contractors solely for that organization's work, on devices
it owns or controls. This includes commercial work performed using OrangeDeck;
it does not include providing OrangeDeck itself to customers or other third
parties as a product or hosted service.

"Modify" means changing the original OrangeDeck code, executable, assets or
documentation. "Derivative work" means a work that adapts, translates or
incorporates copyright-protected portions of OrangeDeck, to the extent that
the result is a derivative work under applicable copyright law.
The permitted activities described in section 2 are not modifications or
derivative works for purposes of these restrictions.

2. Permitted use

You may view and download the source, make the copies needed to compile the
unmodified source, and install and run OrangeDeck on devices you own or
control for your personal or internal use, without a license fee.
An organization may deploy those permitted copies internally for the users
described in section 1.

Changing your settings, connecting your devices, selecting a project or editor,
and creating or editing your own files through the app are permitted. Building
the unmodified source with the supplied installation and build tools is also
permitted. Your own project files and work output are not OrangeDeck merely
because you use the app to work with them.

Keep this license and the applicable third-party notices with permitted copies.
You may share a link to the official OrangeDeck repository or download. You may
also share screenshots to describe or review OrangeDeck, identifying it as
OrangeDeck and respecting the rights in any other material shown.

